title: The transport cannot stream - every follow mode blocks forever
updated: 2026-08-27T06:35:03Z
---

Structural, and the reason several endpoints are only half usable.

_request sends Connection: close, reads the whole response, then parses.
That is fine for a request/response endpoint and wrong for every endpoint
whose point is that it keeps going:

  containers->logs(follow => 1)   never returns
  system->events with no until    never returns
  containers->stats without stream => 0   never returns

Today the only defence is that the caller must bound the window, which the
POD says but nothing enforces. A caller who forgets hangs the process with
no diagnostic.

What a fix looks like: an optional per-request event callback, invoked as
frames or ndjson lines arrive, with _request returning once the callback
says stop or the daemon closes. That keeps the existing buffered path as
the default and makes the follow modes usable without changing any current
signature.

Doing this also unblocks the Upgrade: tcp half of attach and exec, which
needs a live bidirectional connection.

Adjacent, worth a thought while in here: every _request calls _reconnect
and closes afterwards, so there is no connection reuse at all.


